# Issue #2 test matrix - Square (S1-S5) and BERT B4, all pinned to MR32_NR7.
# Square goes up to 5000^3 (~750 GFLOP/rep at N_REPS=5) - this group runs with
# skip_ref_run=true and a reduced iteration count in config.json so a full
# scalar reference GEMM and 1000-rep RVV sweep don't take hours on-board.
#
# Future-work note (issue #7): S1-S5's KerGOPs/pack-vs-compute split all land in the
# same narrow band regardless of problem size (see .scratch/issues/0003-*.md) - the
# Square family's behavior is already captured by S1+S2. S3-S5 are commented out
# (not deleted) to cut board time on future re-runs; re-enable if a future issue
# needs the larger-size data points specifically.
# layer  M      N    K
S1       1000   1000  1000
S2       2000   2000  2000
# S3       3000   3000  3000
# S4       4000   4000  4000
# S5       5000   5000  5000
B4       4096   384   1024
